From 181c60c2d8c668ee423d1435e5fe40f3ba7573b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 22:08:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 50/51] Emoticons in the danmaku chat; chat list scrolls when
 signed out; face verification status over POST
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- An emoticon panel under the chat (dock and floating chat), inside the
  chat window so it works over full-screen apps. It offers the room's
  packs (GetEmoticons) and the account's main-site packs (小黄脸 and owned
  packs); stickers go out with dm_type 1 as their emoticon_unique, main-site
  emotes as "upower_[code]" like the Bilibili apps. Locked ones show how to
  unlock them.
- Chat lines draw inline emoticons and stickers as pictures. Pictures come
  only from Bilibili's image hosts, without cookies, scaled to 160 px PNGs
  in Caches/LiveHime/emoticons (trimmed at 30 MB); at most 16 MB in memory.
- The danmaku page is no longer disabled as a whole when signed out, which
  also stopped the chat list from scrolling.
- IsUserIdentifiedByFaceAuth answers POST only now (GET returns 405). The
  QR face verification window no longer checks the status by itself; the
  user confirms, as before, since the status can report an earlier
  verification.
- Interface check: room and main-site emoticons, face status field names.
- Tests: e2e-emoticons.mjs, the panel over a full-screen app.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
